{
  "abstract": "We determine all rational-function extensions of one populated paired rational Diophantine sextuple over its full elliptic source field. Let $K=\\mathbb Q(n,\\sqrt n,\\sqrt{6n+10},\\sqrt{10n+54})$, and specialize the first paired family of rStation Paper75 to $h=3$. We prove that the only $F\\in K$ whose products with all six entries, increased by one, are squares in $K$ is $F=0$. The proof first determines the complete integral Mordell–Weil group of the elliptic curve induced by three entries: its rank is four and its torsion is $C_4\\times C_2$. Character decomposition, injective specializations and an independent Frobenius computation establish the rank; explicit halves, finite-place Kummer witnesses, exact heights and a congruence argument establish saturation. The six-square product then gives a nonisotrivial genus-two fibration. An explicit semistable resolution has relative canonical square12 and at most24 singular fibres. Tan's effective height inequality bounds every possible elliptic section by Shioda height480. The required coset contains11832 points below this bound up to negation. Thirteen split places over101 eliminate all but the zero extender, with an independent PARI enumeration reproducing every survivor count. The theorem allows arbitrary ordinary poles and arbitrary elliptic coefficients. It excludes no isolated rational specialization, no further source cover, and no moving-parameter or general rational septuple. The supplement contains portable exact certificates and the complete rank-computation inputs and outputs.",
